    "q-181002": {
      "dom_id": "step-q181002",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "The solution to the inequality $-9a\\le -54$ is $a${{field-1}}{{field-2}}.",
      "worked_solution": "The variable $a$ is being *multiplied* by $-9.$ To isolate $a,$ we perform the *opposite* operation, which is *dividing* by $-9.$ Remember to perform the same operation on both sides.\n\nAlso, when multiplying or dividing an inequality by a negative number, we need to flip the inequality sign:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-9a\\,\\, & \\le \\,\\,-54 \\\\ \\frac{-9a}{-9}\\,\\, & \\ge \\,\\,\\frac{-54}{-9} \\\\ \\frac{-9a}{-9}\\,\\, & \\ge \\,\\,6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can cancel a common factor of $-9$ from both the numerator and denominator.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-9a}{-9} & \\ge 6 \\\\ \\frac{\\cancel{-9}a}{\\cancel{-9}} & \\ge 6 \\\\ a & \\ge 6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $a\\ge 6.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
